{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-78965" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate $\\int \\frac{{log}_{3}⁡(2x)}{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042880/state.json" "file_sha256" "ab26108ee4385b404b58e77caec20dfbc88367a8189a20b676af44928aa91217"} {"question" "q-78965" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We will solve this problem using integration by parts. We start by defining $u$ and ${v}^{′},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u={log}_{3}⁡(2x)\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡3} \\\\ {v}^{′}=\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int \\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x=-\\frac{1}{x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{{log}_{3}⁡(2x)}{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={log}_{3}⁡(2x)\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{x})-\\int (-\\frac{1}{x})(\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡3})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{{log}_{3}⁡(2x)}{x}-\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}\\int -\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{{log}_{3}⁡(2x)}{x}-\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}+C \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x)}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}-\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}+C \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x)+1}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is an integral constant.\n\nNote that in the above calculation we used the change of base formula ${log}_{3}⁡x=\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042880/state.json" "file_sha256" "ab26108ee4385b404b58e77caec20dfbc88367a8189a20b676af44928aa91217"} {"question" "q-78965" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042880/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "945b955513bd043cb1ea5613b6552b6255996e206cbfd655b769cfe82c47535f"} {"question" "q-78965" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042880/state.json" "file_sha256" "ab26108ee4385b404b58e77caec20dfbc88367a8189a20b676af44928aa91217"} {"question" "q-78965" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x)+1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}+C"] ["math" "-\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x)+1}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}+C"] ["math" "\\frac{1-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x)}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}+C"] ["math" "\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x)+1}{{x}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}+C"] ["math" "\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x)-1}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}+C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042880/state.json" "file_sha256" "ab26108ee4385b404b58e77caec20dfbc88367a8189a20b676af44928aa91217"} {"question" "q-78965" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x)+1}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}+C"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042880/state.json" "file_sha256" "ab26108ee4385b404b58e77caec20dfbc88367a8189a20b676af44928aa91217"} {"question" "q-114551" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate $\\int 9{x}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042880/state.json" "file_sha256" "ab26108ee4385b404b58e77caec20dfbc88367a8189a20b676af44928aa91217"} {"question" "q-114551" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We will solve this problem using integration by parts. We start by defining $u$ and ${v}^{′},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x)\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=\\frac{1}{x} \\\\ {v}^{′}=9{x}^{2}\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int 9{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x=3{x}^{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 9{x}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x)(3{x}^{3})-\\int \\frac{3{x}^{3}}{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3{x}^{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x)-3\\int {x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3{x}^{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-{x}^{3}+C \\\\  & ={x}^{3}(3\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-1)+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is an integral constant." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042880/state.json" "file_sha256" "ab26108ee4385b404b58e77caec20dfbc88367a8189a20b676af44928aa91217"} {"question" "q-114551" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042880/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "945b955513bd043cb1ea5613b6552b6255996e206cbfd655b769cfe82c47535f"} {"question" "q-114551" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042880/state.json" "file_sha256" "ab26108ee4385b404b58e77caec20dfbc88367a8189a20b676af44928aa91217"} {"question" "q-114551" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2{x}^{3}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+1)+C"] ["math" "2{x}^{3}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-3)+C"] ["math" "{x}^{3}(2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-3)+C"] ["math" "{x}^{3}(3\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-1)+C"] ["math" "{x}^{3}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-2)+C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042880/state.json" "file_sha256" "ab26108ee4385b404b58e77caec20dfbc88367a8189a20b676af44928aa91217"} {"question" "q-114551" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{x}^{3}(3\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-1)+C"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042880/state.json" "file_sha256" "ab26108ee4385b404b58e77caec20dfbc88367a8189a20b676af44928aa91217"} {"question" "q-114552" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate $\\int 2x{log}_{5}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042880/state.json" "file_sha256" "ab26108ee4385b404b58e77caec20dfbc88367a8189a20b676af44928aa91217"} {"question" "q-114552" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We will solve this problem using integration by parts. We start by defining $u$ and ${v}^{′},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u={log}_{5}⁡(x)\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡5} \\\\ {v}^{′}=2x\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int 2x\\,\\text{d}x={x}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 2x{log}_{5}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={log}_{5}⁡(x)({x}^{2})-\\int ({x}^{2})(\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡5})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={x}^{2}{log}_{5}⁡(x)-\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}\\int x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={x}^{2}{log}_{5}⁡(x)-\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}\\cdot \\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}(2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-1)+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is an integral constant.\n\nNote that in the above calculation we used the change of base formula ${log}_{5}⁡x=\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042880/state.json" "file_sha256" "ab26108ee4385b404b58e77caec20dfbc88367a8189a20b676af44928aa91217"} {"question" "q-114552" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042880/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "945b955513bd043cb1ea5613b6552b6255996e206cbfd655b769cfe82c47535f"} {"question" "q-114552" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042880/state.json" "file_sha256" "ab26108ee4385b404b58e77caec20dfbc88367a8189a20b676af44928aa91217"} {"question" "q-114552" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}(2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-1)+C"] ["math" "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}(3\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+2)+C"] ["math" "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}(4\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+1)+C"] ["math" "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}(4\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-1)+C"] ["math" "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-1)+C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042880/state.json" "file_sha256" "ab26108ee4385b404b58e77caec20dfbc88367a8189a20b676af44928aa91217"} {"question" "q-114552" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}(2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-1)+C"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042880/state.json" "file_sha256" "ab26108ee4385b404b58e77caec20dfbc88367a8189a20b676af44928aa91217"} {"question" "q-114679" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate ${\\int }_{1/2}^{1}{log}_{3}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042880/state.json" "file_sha256" "ab26108ee4385b404b58e77caec20dfbc88367a8189a20b676af44928aa91217"} {"question" "q-114679" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we write the integral as\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{1/2}^{1}{log}_{3}⁡(2x)\\text{d}x={\\int }_{1/2}^{1}\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x)}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}{\\int }_{1/2}^{1}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x)\\cdot 1\\cdot \\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe will solve this problem using integration by parts. We start by defining $u$ and ${v}^{′},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x)\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=\\frac{1}{x} \\\\ {v}^{′}=1\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int 1\\cdot \\,dx=x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1/2}^{1}{log}_{3}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}{\\int }_{1/2}^{1}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x)\\cdot 1\\cdot \\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}{\\int }_{1/2}^{1}u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}[uv{|}_{1/2}^{1}-{\\int }_{1/2}^{1}v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}[x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x){|}_{1/2}^{1}-{\\int }_{1/2}^{1}x(\\frac{1}{x})\\,\\text{d}x] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}[1\\cdot \\operatorname{ln}⁡(2\\cdot 1)-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2\\cdot \\frac{1}{2})-{\\int }_{1/2}^{1}\\,\\text{d}x] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}[\\operatorname{ln}⁡2-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡1-x{|}_{1/2}^{1}\\,] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}[\\operatorname{ln}⁡2-0-(1-\\frac{1}{2})] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}[\\operatorname{ln}⁡2-\\frac{1}{2}] \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2-1}{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042880/state.json" "file_sha256" "ab26108ee4385b404b58e77caec20dfbc88367a8189a20b676af44928aa91217"} {"question" "q-114679" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042880/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "945b955513bd043cb1ea5613b6552b6255996e206cbfd655b769cfe82c47535f"} {"question" "q-114679" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042880/state.json" "file_sha256" "ab26108ee4385b404b58e77caec20dfbc88367a8189a20b676af44928aa91217"} {"question" "q-114679" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2+1}{3\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}"] ["math" "\\frac{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2-1}{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}"] ["math" "\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2+1}{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}"] ["math" "\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2-1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}"] ["math" "\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042880/state.json" "file_sha256" "ab26108ee4385b404b58e77caec20dfbc88367a8189a20b676af44928aa91217"} {"question" "q-114679" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2-1}{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042880/state.json" "file_sha256" "ab26108ee4385b404b58e77caec20dfbc88367a8189a20b676af44928aa91217"} {"question" "q-350976" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{1/10}^{e/10}{log}_{5}⁡(10x)\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042880/state.json" "file_sha256" "ab26108ee4385b404b58e77caec20dfbc88367a8189a20b676af44928aa91217"} {"question" "q-350976" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we write the integral as\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{1/10}^{e/10}{log}_{5}⁡(10x)\\,\\text{d}x={\\int }_{1/10}^{e/10}{log}_{5}⁡(10x)\\cdot 1\\cdot \\text{d}x.\n$$\n\n \n\nWe will solve this problem using integration by parts. We start by defining $u$ and ${v}^{′},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u={log}_{5}⁡(10x)\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5)} \\\\ {v}^{′}=1\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int 1\\cdot \\,dx=x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1/10}^{e/10}{log}_{5}⁡(10x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{1/10}^{e/10}u{v}^{′}\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv{|}_{1/10}^{e/10}-{\\int }_{1/10}^{e/10}v{u}^{′}\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={log}_{5}⁡(10x)\\,(x){|}_{1/10}^{e/10}-{\\int }_{1/10}^{e/10}x(\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5)})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =[{log}_{5}⁡(10\\cdot \\frac{e}{10})\\,(\\frac{e}{10})-{log}_{5}⁡(10\\cdot \\frac{1}{10})\\,(\\frac{1}{10})]-\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5)}{\\int }_{1/10}^{e/10}\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{e}{10}{log}_{5}⁡(e)-\\frac{1}{10}{log}_{5}⁡(1)-\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5)}x{|}_{1/10}^{e/10} \\\\  & =\\frac{e}{10}\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5)}-\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5)}(\\frac{e}{10}-\\frac{1}{10}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{10\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042880/state.json" "file_sha256" "ab26108ee4385b404b58e77caec20dfbc88367a8189a20b676af44928aa91217"} {"question" "q-350976" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042880/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "945b955513bd043cb1ea5613b6552b6255996e206cbfd655b769cfe82c47535f"} {"question" "q-350976" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042880/state.json" "file_sha256" "ab26108ee4385b404b58e77caec20dfbc88367a8189a20b676af44928aa91217"} {"question" "q-350976" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{10\\ln(5)}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042880/state.json" "file_sha256" "ab26108ee4385b404b58e77caec20dfbc88367a8189a20b676af44928aa91217"}] "usage" {} "basis" 1583 "retractions" [] "immutable_answers" [] "immutable_fields" [] "no_history" []}
